{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36723-running-the-end-of-the-world-how-you-did-it","id":36723,"title":"Running the End of The World, How you did it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-24T20:41:51-08:00","id":36723,"title":"Running the End of The World, How you did it?","content":"some of us have done it, some others havent.<br /> on my case im interested in using the characters from the Book of Revelations translated to my players, for each one to represent something and end up with a proper armagedon (though i dont know if i should incorporate God...and or if i use it, should be the one that supposedly appears on Wraith)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T11:33:06-08:00","id":40077,"title":"","content":"I never ran it but if I did it would be very bleak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:37:03-08:00","id":40135,"title":"","content":"Depends on which gamelines are involved. I might (or might not) go with something Biblical if running a <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> end of the world; but I probably wouldn\u2019t if running a <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> Apocalypse. I once tried to sew together all of the gamelines into one epic finish, weaving together all of the <b>Time of Judgment</b> books plus <b>Orpheus</b>; it was a glorious mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:41:56-08:00","id":40214,"title":"","content":"how was orpheus ending?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T19:05:58-08:00","id":40291,"title":"","content":"Well basically <i>End Game</i>, the final Orpheus book sees the PCs finally crossing the Stormwall and seeing the Underworld for the first time. At the same time there's a Spectre War going on between Grandmother and a group of Malfeans opposing her, realizing that she will eventually consume <b><i>everything</i> </b>if she isn't stopped. They'll actually offer an alliance with the projectors against Grandmother, whether they take it is up to the players but regardless the central goal is the same, find a way to stop Grandmother.<br /> <br /> The book presents a couple different ways of stopping Grandmother, the one stands out the most and likely the one Data's thinking about is tracking down something Grandmother fears and has hidden away in a memory tower. As it turns out that something is Abel, <i>the</i> Abel. Not only that but because of what he is, the first murder victim and all those who followed him, he's become a sort of gateway between the worlds of the dead and the living. With that power he can channel a large amount of lifeforce from the living world into Grandmother directly which will either obliterate Grandmother completely or sate her hunger and put her back to sleep. The catch, it will take a large sacrifice of life to do that. Two of possibilities they suggest is the entire Amazon rainforest or a major city like London, Tokyo or Hong Kong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T12:54:57-08:00","id":40657,"title":"","content":"I've been rereading Chapter 4 Kindred of the East: Interesting Times from &quot;Time of Judgement&quot;. I've been thinking it would be fun to weave together elements of the four scenarios presented and dump it on everyone in the East; i.e. China, Japan, India, Mongolia, Tibet, Indonesia, Indochina, Myanmar, Thailand, etc., regardless of their being Werewolf, Mage, Demon or Hunter. I'ld slam the rest of the world with Chapter 1 Changeling the Dreaming: Endless Winter. I'm partial to the idea of &quot;yes; it's the apocalypse, but it's not the one you were waiting for.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T03:42:31-08:00","id":42797,"title":"","content":"I'd run it that the Antes and Caines comes back to throw the world into a new Dark Age after which there is a grand judgment where Caine delivers Old Testament style justice to his grandchilder and let them suffer - a lot.<br /> <br /> But since I am more into Dark Ages I think that I would let Gehenna hit around 1500 or so rather than around the 20-21the century shift. That way I can keep my Dark Ages stuff and not let them get bogged down with the kind of things that don't interest me at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T21:28:59-08:00","id":43337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36723-running-the-end-of-the-world-how-you-did-it?p=42797#post42797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But since I am more into Dark Ages I think that I would let Gehenna hit around 1500 or so rather than around the 20-21the century shift. That way I can keep my Dark Ages stuff and not let them get bogged down with the kind of things that don't interest me at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an interesting idea. You'd have less problems since disbelief/the Weaver is weaker, but also a less stuff to work with. Given all the stuff that had to be used to stop the Ravnos Anti.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T05:10:23-08:00","id":43448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36723-running-the-end-of-the-world-how-you-did-it?p=43337#post43337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like an interesting idea. You'd have less problems since disbelief/the Weaver is weaker, but also a less stuff to work with. Given all the stuff that had to be used to stop the Ravnos Anti.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Can't say that I am up to date on the Werewolf and Mage stuff and all, but I won't mind the Cainites dominating the playfield. After all, I'm mostly into vampire when it comes to OWoD. But you are right that it will require some significent force to tackle on the Antes with the present technological arsenal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T18:11:34-08:00","id":45263,"title":"","content":"Mine ended with the birth of a new God. She restored reality (more or less) after it ended, but she didn't quite make it the same as before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T22:41:38-08:00","id":52157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sidious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36723-running-the-end-of-the-world-how-you-did-it?p=45263#post45263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mine ended with the birth of a new God. She restored reality (more or less) after it ended, but she didn't quite make it the same as before.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way? (Out of curiosity.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:33:05-08:00","id":52364,"title":"","content":"Well after the new God took over she basically hand waved reality. I incorporated the parts of the Gehenna stories I liked. Had reality crumbling from Wormwood and eventually it all came down to Lucifer, Lilith, and Cain having a conversation. They pretty much realized they had been twats for eons. But since the Father was gone (dead, left, up in the air) they couldn't atone for it. They realized the girl with the tattoo was marked to ascend to divinity and needed the push. so ritual, and much talking and convincing later she became the new God and put the world back to rights with a few changes since she wasn't the original creator.<br /> <br /> Around this time Requiem was making the big splash and some players wanted to try out some of the clans but weren't thrilled with the new system. Seeing some things I, myself, liked I figured It be a good time to incorporate some of the changes. I also kept some of the effects of Gehenna going for those that survived up to that point (blood bonds broke, humanity grew/decreased, etc).<br /> <br /> The players woke up the next day (they were vampires, important note). Roll WP. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Depending on the successes on the roll, they had reactions ranging from Nothing new here, something feels wrong, But that's not how THAT happened, I remember everything!. Some characters woke up in new clans (one wanted to play a Daeva), Some had new clan weaknesses (I used the new Gangrel weakness), and some had new allies, I ported over a few of the new clans (made them children of Lilith, not that players knew that), The Garou all changed into Forsaken, at least minorly (never did finish that conversion, huh.) Things like that.<br /> <br /> Things continued and there was a subtle shift in Kindred society. After the initial few sessions I fast forwarded the game a couple of years and had the Cam and Sabbat fall apart and it became more of a Dark Ages vampire society. Princes had their own domain and ruled it. No over arching governing body of vampires. Most keep the simple rules but it was all very decentralized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T06:58:24-08:00","id":62885,"title":"","content":"I would probably do it as the end of the world as we know it, rather than the literal end of the world. The antediluvians would simply wake up and behave as they normally did in times past. Of course this would lead to masquerade shattering proxies wars as they use all the technological and supernatural means at the disposal of their followers.<br /> <br /> Ravanna would lead the Ravnos against the Kuei-jin and this would culminate in full scale war between India and China. Haqim would lead the Assamites in a war against all other kindred, using islamic extremists as convenient dupes where possible. Ennoia would lead the Gangrel on a massive eco-terrorist campaign. Salout would take over the Tremere from the inside, while his childer Shaitan would arise in Mexico City having subverted the Regent and inner circle of the Sabbat, and the Baali wars would begin anew.<br /> <br /> Ventrue would awaken and become the dominant force in the crumbling Camarilla, aided by Arikel. Cappadocius will escape from the underworld with the Harbingers of Skulls and lead them against the GIovanni. Lasombra will emerge from the abyss to lead the antitribu to vengeance against the rest of the Clan.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce will go all Deep Rising on NYC spawning horrific monsters and devouring tens of thousands before retreating into the ocean like some kind of twisted Kaiju. Brujah will appear from the depths of time and led his childer against Triole's. Absimiliard will hound his descendants to the four corners of the Earth with the Nictuku. Malkav will rise from torpor and reveal he has been psychically directing the clan through the Madness network and begins a Jokeresque reign of chaos, his childer committing mass practical jokes and terrorism in equal measure. Set would return to wage war on the Children of Osiris and the mummies of Horus.<br /> <br /> To accomplish these goals, the antediluvian would be siring numerous new childer along the way, and scores of 4th generation neonates would be running around.<br /> <br /> Of course the Lupines and Mages will be going beserk at these developments and in the end, all this blatant supernatural carnage will shatter the masquerade so hard that the Dreaming will reintegrate with the world and the world will end up becoming a post-apocalyptic mishmash of high technology and fantastical magic and monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T09:58:32-08:00","id":62961,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy would especially be going nuts since this is a huge reality breech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T10:36:44-08:00","id":62988,"title":"","content":"I ran an end of days chronicle for my mage the ascension chronicle of two years, believe it or not it was more inspired by the cover of the book Ascension than anything else, essentially the nephandi decided it was time to play their trump card and unleash oblivion, I can't do the concept justice in a short post but basically the physical world started to cease to exist and reality became very unstable, the players eventually saved the world and stopped the nephandi and their dark masters who ultimately destroyed themselves, it was a pretty cool game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T17:35:32-08:00","id":63662,"title":"","content":"This wasn't a game I was a part of but a friend was and she told me about it the other day. Basically it began with ominous stories and rumors involving the Tremere and the Tzimisce. The leadership of the Tremere suddenly thrown into disarray with many elders recalled to Vienna. What few knew was that Saulot had finally bested [Tremere's], claiming his body for his own and killing after the Inner Council in the process. Tzimisce elders were disappearing, enraging the Sabbat who believed the Camarilla and Anarchs were behind it, increasing the tension between the Sects and leading to skirmishes and small scale war between them. And all kinds of other dark portents.<br /> <br /> Eventually [Tzimisce] rose up in New York-like in the picture of him in <i>Gehenna</i>-and consumed/absorbed over half the city's population in a night before disappearing. When this happened everything started falling apart. The Masquerade rapidly crumbled and the Camarilla freaked out at what had happened to New York while the Sabbat were rallying to war, doing anything and everything to prepare mortals be damned.<br /> <br /> The PCs had actually started off in the New York and survived [Tzimisce's] return, saved from death by Saulot and the seven Salubri. Saulot explained to them his history with [Tzimisce], twin brothers in life but destined to be enemies in unlife, claiming that a lost fragment of the Book of Nod prophetized that they would one day wage war on one another for the fate of all Cainites. And of course [Tzimisce] knows this as well as been plotting and preparing for this moment for eons. Through a convoluted scheme he spread his essence through nearly his entire Clan with each Tzimisce unknowingly carrying and nurturing a sliver of him. Once the Clan had grown and spread out enough he would rise and consume them all, reabsorbing his lost pieces and growing stronger, hoping to become God in form and power. Of course it wasn't just his Clan and its Bloodlines but Tzimisce revenant families, the Tremere and Tzimisce Gargoyles as well as anyone that had dablerized a Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The PCs went off on this globe-trotting, race-against-time adventure to locate things Saulot needed for a ritual to help him destroy [Tzimisce] and in the end bore witness to this huge apocalyptic battle Saulot and [Tzimisce]. Of course in true Antediluvian fashion Saulot was scheming to absorb [Tzimisce] and become God or at least God-like. Fortunately, Kartarirya, the first and last of [Tzimisce's] Childer, aided the PCs in messing with the ritual, destroying the two of them as Saulot was consuming his brother destroying them both in a wave of magical backlash. Somehow they actually survived the whole thing though the world was pretty much shattered by the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T10:26:30-08:00","id":64960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36723-running-the-end-of-the-world-how-you-did-it?p=62961#post62961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy would especially be going nuts since this is a huge reality breech.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of them as antagonists for a different sort of endgame.<br /> <br /> Instead of the antediluvians arising to war on each other, or to devour their descendants, you could have Caine receive oracular visions while in torpor, of the Technocracy eventually conquering the world centuries down the line and purging it of all things supernatural including vampires. That's not acceptable to him, his progeny must continue to &quot;live&quot; and suffer as long as he see fit. To prevent this he uses Speak Through the Blood and gives a simple order, destroy the technocracy. <br /> <br /> Suddenly, those of the seventh generation down to the Antediluvians themselves find themselves &quot;realizing&quot; what a threat these mages are and plotting against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T14:52:39-08:00","id":65985,"title":"","content":"That's a neat idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T16:13:14-08:00","id":66821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/36723-running-the-end-of-the-world-how-you-did-it?p=65985#post65985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a neat idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I was thinking that would be a campaign best played by ancillae of the 8th and 9th generation who've been around for a while (maybe 100-150 years), and them trying to understand what going on with this unnatural whiplash in policy by the elders of all clans and sects. It would be part war story, part mystery as they delve into the reality that they truly bear a biblical curse that leaves them puppets to an ancient monster's whims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T22:43:21-08:00","id":71057,"title":"","content":"I never ran it, but if I did, I'd start with an earthquake...birds and snakes...an aeroplane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}